================================================================================
TEST T44988 -- ACL: Hardware MAC 4000 range, applied to ports
================================================================================
Run:      2026-10-09, box local time (device clocks were set to box local time
          during setup, so device and host stamps are comparable)
Bench:    tb277, consoles u2, u3, u5; Test Engineer bidhanc@bidhanc-dl
Tester:   bench-runner
Graded:   tester
Case:     AWP-8616, objective "a numbered hardware MAC access-list in the 4000
          range filters on source and destination MAC address when applied to a
          port with access-group", 7 steps as run
Build:    swi_c  sin_x96056-20260921-9 (netboots)
          swi_b  sin_x96056-20260921-9 (AT-x960-28YSQ, console u3)
Configs:  swi_c.cfg, swi_b.cfg (running-config after setup; saved to startup: no)

VERDICT: PASS -- numbered hardware MAC ACLs in the 4000 range bind to a port with
         `access-group` and filter on source and destination MAC, with wildcard mask
         semantics, the vlan qualifier and copy-to-cpu all proven by measurement.
      4000-range MAC list accepted .... yes        (stored as "Hardware MAC access list 4000")
      bound to a port ................. works      (access-group 4000 on port1.0.48)
      matching src/dst MAC pair ....... denied     (100% packet loss; Packet Hits: 6)
      mask is a WILDCARD .............. proven     (1 = don't care, from both directions)
      zero-mask control ............... matches nothing (list 4001: 0 hits, 0% loss)
      `any` forms ..................... work       (deny any any: 100% loss, 3 hits)
      vlan qualifier .................. selects    (vlan 100 denies, vlan 1 does not)
      copy-to-cpu, both halves ........ correct    (CPU queue 0 0->9 = 9 hits, ping 0% loss)
      syntax of the 4000 range ........ measured   (src/mask dst/mask [vlan|inner-vlan|
                                                    tunnel-terminated])
      removal ......................... clean      (each `no access-group` restored traffic)
CAVEAT:  Everything was measured on a VLAN 100 ACCESS port (port1.0.48), the bench's
         deterministic path. The case's stored steps illustrate the feature on a TRUNK port
         carrying VLAN 600; a trunk was not configured, so the `inner-vlan` and
         `tunnel-terminated` qualifiers seen in the syntax were not exercised, and the vlan
         qualifier was proven on VLAN 100 rather than VLAN 600. The frames carried IP/ICMP
         throughout -- a MAC rule was never offered a non-IP ethertype -- and the spoofed
         source MAC 02:00:00:00:00:99 was synthetic, generated on the host rather than
         emitted by a real device. Only the ingress direction was measured.

